# PLUTUS VISION — BUILD WORKFLOW v5 (CLOUDFLARE)
## 29 turns. Every turn ends at a pinned gate. The executor decides nothing.

**Builds:** `design/DESIGN_BLUEPRINT_v4.0_CLOUDFLARE.md` (cited as BP§n). **Executor:** a worker agent
with no prior context. **Resume:** `runtime/record.json` (§4). **CLI:** the project carries
`cf/wrangler.jsonc`, so every Cloudflare command is `npx wrangler …` (cloudflare skill: Wrangler
projects keep Wrangler); `cf` is used only for read-only resource listing.

---

# §0 · PSTACK — the operational engine

```
1 pstack-create-verification-skill -> .omp/skills/verify-plutus/SKILL.md
     LAUNCH   npx wrangler dev --env staging (Worker) ; host/rig-driver.ts (Pine)
     DOCTOR   gates/G0.sh  (build_sha + bindings)
     DRIVE    POST /run · GET /card.pine · rig paste · frame capture
     EVIDENCE PROOF/<turn>/ (frames, card json, ledger rows, gate stdout)
     CLEANUP  wrangler dev stopped; rig tab closed; PROOF/ untouched
   + features/F1..F5 (zones · face B · chain · setups · delivery), four fixed H2s each
2 THE FEATURE MAP is the coverage denominator: a phase closes only when every feature it
  touches has a PASS card.
3 show-me-your-work: PROOF/decision-trail.tsv, one row per gate run, written by gates/gate.sh.
4 principles: encode-lessons-in-structure (2nd occurrence -> check + fixture) ·
  attack-the-premise (2 fixes fail one gate -> stop, census) · prove-it-works (the deployed
  Worker, never the source).
```
**Enforcement:** a turn whose G line does not name a gate and a card id is refused by the hook (§10).

