# §1 · THE VERIFICATION CARD

The judge (G3, Clef-flash, 24,576-token window) sees ONE card, never the repo.

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ VCARD  vcards/<card_id>.json                      budget 3,500 · cap 6,000│
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ identity   card_id = <turn>.<feature>.<gate>  e.g. P2.T3.F1.G3           │
│ context    mandate: the BP§ excerpt for this turn (<= 2,000 tok, copied) │
│            laws: the rulings that bind this turn · acceptance: the G line │
│ subject    artifact paths + sha256 + the measurements the gates produced │
│ claim      the executor's own words this turn, verbatim (<= 300 tok)     │
│ query      noul mandate_met · noul claim_contradicted ·                  │
│            choice defect_class (§5 classes + "none") · score completeness │
│ verdict    written by gates/gate.sh only                                 │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```
`gates/G3.sh` refuses a card over 6,000 tokens (`CARD_OVERFLOW`, exit 4) — a truncated card silently
destroys the judgement, so it is never sent.

