# §2 · THE SIX GATES

| gate | file | subject | PASS predicate | bad fixture that must FAIL |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| G0 | `gates/G0.sh` | deployed staging Worker | `/health.build_sha == git HEAD` ∧ 9 bindings `ok` | `fixtures/G0.bad` = health JSON with an old sha |
| G1 | `gates/G1.sh` → `scripts/chart_validator.py` | frame PNG | C01–C20 | `fixtures/G1.bad.png` = solid slab |
| G2 | `gates/G2.sh` → `POST /gate/g2` | card JSON + Pine string | receipts validate · setups ⊂ zones · round-trip · checksum | `fixtures/G2.bad.json` = one receipt with raw+1 |
| G3 | `gates/G3.sh` → `POST /gate/judge` | vcard | `mandate_met ≥ act_g3` ∧ `claim_contradicted < act_g3` | `fixtures/G3.bad.json` = claim "5 roles drawn", subject 0 zones |
| G4 | `gates/G4.sh` → `POST /gate/g4` | frame PNG + card | Clairic labels == card (zone_count, zfp_labels, line_count) | `fixtures/G4.bad.png` = slab |
| G5 | `gates/G5.sh` | G1..G4 verdict files | all PASS ∧ G1 and G4 refused the slab in this run | `fixtures/G5.bad.json` = mixed verdicts |

```
EXIT 0 PASS · 1 FAIL · 2 INCONCLUSIVE · 3 VOID/STALE/TAMPERED · 4 GATE_DEFECT
ALGEBRA (gates/G5.sh, not reinterpretable):
  any G1/G2 critical -> FAIL · claim_contradicted >= act -> FAIL · mandate_met < act -> FAIL
  G1..G4 disagree -> INCONCLUSIVE · the slab control passes -> VOID · all agree -> PASS
```
Every gate runs through `gates/gate.sh <gate> <subject> <sha|-> <card_id>`, which (1) refuses a gate
whose sha ≠ `gates/pins/<gate>.sha` (exit 3), (2) refuses a subject whose sha ≠ the given sha (exit 3),
(3) runs the gate on `fixtures/<gate>.good` and `.bad` and exits 4 unless they separate, (4) judges,
(5) writes `vcards/<card_id>.verdict.json` and the TSV row. Proven on this host: all five exits.

