# §4 · THE LOOP

```
OUTER  read runtime/record.json -> run next_command -> the turn's A/E -> its G
       rc 0  gate wrote verdict + TSV; set record.turn = next; commit (C line)
       rc 1  read vcards/<id>.verdict.json defect_class -> §5 owner file -> fix -> same G, same subject
       rc 2  supply the missing input named in stdout; never re-run blind
       rc 3  the subject moved or the gate changed: re-capture / re-pin (pins change only at P0)
       rc 4  the gate cannot separate its fixtures: repair the GATE, never the subject
INNER  every gate run: pin check -> subject sha -> good/bad separation -> judge -> verdict
DONE   P5 replay PASS on the frozen BUILD_SHA. Nothing the executor says closes a phase.
```
`runtime/record.json`:
```json
{"phase":"P0","turn":"P0.T0","last_pass_card":null,"frozen_build_sha":null,
 "next_command":"see §11 P0.T0 A","blocked":[]}
```

