# §6 · LAWS

```
1 a gate's subject is the deployed artifact or its emitted output — never its own source
2 a gate accepts its good fixture and refuses its bad one on every run
3 a verdict comes from the artifact — never prose, a count, a filename, a status field
4 the executor runs gates; it never edits a pinned gate, never writes a verdict
5 every phase exits on a judged artifact
6 the trail is written as the run happens
```

# §7 · DEBUG

FAIL → class → owner file → same gate on the same subject. Max 3 rounds per gate. A fix that turns
another check red is a regression: restore, narrow.

# §8 · FORBIDDEN (injected verbatim into every turn prompt by the runner)

```
advance on a red gate                          weaken or lower a gate to pass it
reuse evidence produced before a fix           describe an artifact you did not open
report a count/sha/suite/token as a verdict    let a filename assert a verdict
edit a pinned gate during the build            write the verdict you are judged by
pass the corpus to the judge instead of a card set a threshold without pv-calibrate
declare done without a frozen-artifact PASS    skip the control because it "always" passes
add a fallback, default, or substitute value   build anything not named in the turn's A line
```

# §9 · CHECKS THAT EARN THEIR PLACE

`deploy equality` (G0) · `subject sha` (gate.sh) · `control separation` (gate.sh) · `card budget` (G3)
· `region control` (G1 C-checks on the zone area, not the whole frame) · `substitute value` (firewall
D10) · `side effect outside a step` (firewall D11) · `byte step result` (firewall D12) · `scope before a
zero` (every count printed with its R2 prefix / D1 query).

# §10 · MECHANICAL BLOCKING

```
gates/gate.sh            the only runner; exit 0..4
gates/pins/*.sha         a changed gate exits 3 before judging
gates/firewall.sh        D1..D12, one command, nonzero = refused
.githooks/pre-commit     refuses a commit touching cf/src pine/ host/ unless
                         PROOF/decision-trail.tsv has a code-0 row for the card id named
                         in the commit body (line "card: <id>")
                         WIRED ONLY BY `upper attach <project path>` (jarvis-upper), which sets the
                         hooks path AND asserts the directory exists and the hook is executable.
                         Setting the hooks path by hand is forbidden: a path to a missing directory
                         runs nothing, silently.
runtime/record.json      the resumable state
```
Firewall detectors added in P0.T6 (names fixed now):
```
D9  catch-swallow     grep -rnE 'catch *\([^)]*\) *\{ *(return|\})' cf/src/{e1,e2,e3,steps,workflow}
D10 substitute value  grep -rnE '\?\? *(0|""|\[\]|false|null|NaN)\b|\|\| *(0|"")' cf/src/{e1,e2,e3,steps,workflow}
D11 write outside step  scripts/lint-steps.ts: env.R2.put|env.D1|LEDGER|WEEK_SEAL only inside step.do callbacks
D12 byte step result  scripts/lint-steps.ts: no step.do callback returns Uint8Array|ArrayBuffer
```

